<!--Post: 10893--><!--Time: 1110268113-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10893"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Raedelina<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Raedelina<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 11:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is just another &#34;Zynchronicitiy&#34; that seems to have followed me lately.  I grew up reading and participating in GAMES Magazine.  My mother was very active in cultivating the &#34;gifted&#34; side of my and my brother&#39;s intellects.  I felt very special for being interested in this magazine even then... at age 8 or 9.  I am still obsessed with languages, numbers, patterns and symmetry.  I still worship this mag. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
