<!--Post: 10894--><!--Time: 1110269457-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10894"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Raedelina<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Raedelina<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 12:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry to double post, but I am trying to follow my own &#40;rapidly escalating&#41; stream of consciousness.   <BR> <BR>ONLY certain types are interested in this magazine.  I am 32 years old and probably have the old issue in question in storage at my parents.  I have studied several other languages and I get a weird, &#34;The Shining&#34; sort of vibe with Rader, according to the language and &#34;coding&#34; he has chosen to follow.  It is not only symbolic but literal as well.   <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
